# Frontend Conventions

## Component Standards

- All components are **functional** with hooks. Use `.jsx` for JSX files.
- One default export per file. Co-locate state with the component that owns it.
- Destructure props and context values at the top of the component.
- Avoid `useEffect` with missing dependencies – always declare full dependency arrays.

## Context Usage

Two contexts exist. Use the right one:

```jsx
// Auth state – login/logout/user object
import { useAuthContext } from "../context/AuthContext";
const { user, loading, login, logout } = useAuthContext();

// App data – user profile, posts, socket
import { useContext } from "react";
import { UserDataContext, socket } from "../context/UserContext";
const { userData, allPostsData, profileData, editProfile, setEditProfile, handleGetProfile, getCurrentUser, getAllPosts } = useContext(UserDataContext);
```

`AuthProvider` wraps the entire app. `UserContextProvider` wraps only private routes.
**Never** access `UserDataContext` inside `AuthProvider` directly or outside `PrivateRoute`.

## API Calls – Always Use `apiHelpers`

Never use raw `axios` in components. Use the shared instance which auto-injects the Bearer token:

```js
import apiHelpers from "../../api/apiHelper";

// GET
const res = await apiHelpers.get("/user/suggest-users", { withCredentials: true });

// POST (JSON)
const res = await apiHelpers.post("/connection/send/:id", {}, { withCredentials: true });

// POST (multipart)
const form = new FormData();
form.append("image", file);
form.append("description", text);
const res = await apiHelpers.post("/post/create-post", form, { withCredentials: true });

// DELETE
const res = await apiHelpers.delete("/connection/remove/:userId", { withCredentials: true });
```

`apiHelpers` returns `response.data` directly – no `.data` unwrapping needed.
All error toasts are shown automatically by the response interceptor.

## Route Protection

```jsx
// PrivateRoute – redirects unauthenticated users to /login
// PublicRoute  – redirects authenticated users to /

// Both respect AuthContext.loading (show loading div until auth resolves)
```

Pages: `/ HomePage` · `/network` · `/profile` · `/notifications` → private  
Pages: `/login` · `/signup` → public

## Navigate to a User Profile

Always use `handleGetProfile` from context – it fetches data and navigates:

```jsx
const { handleGetProfile } = useContext(UserDataContext);
const navigate = useNavigate();

handleGetProfile(user.userName, navigate); // fetches profile + goes to /profile
```

## Toast Notifications

```js
import toast from "react-hot-toast";
toast.success("Post created!");
toast.error("Something went wrong.");
// Toaster is already in App.jsx (top-right, 3000ms)
```

## Socket Listeners

The global `socket` from `UserContext` is for post events (likes, comments).
Clean up every listener in the `useEffect` return:

```jsx
import { socket } from "../context/UserContext";

useEffect(() => {
  socket.on("likeUpdated", ({ postId, likes }) => { if (postId === id) setLikes(likes); });
  return () => { socket.off("likeUpdated"); };
}, [id]);
```

The `Chatbot` and `ConnectionButton` components each create their own separate socket connection.

## Rendering Markdown

Post descriptions and comments support Markdown:

```jsx
import ReactMarkdown from "react-markdown";

<div className="prose dark:prose-invert">
  <ReactMarkdown>{content}</ReactMarkdown>
</div>
```

## Image Fallback

```jsx
import emptyDp from "../assets/emptyDp.jpg";
<img src={user.profileImage || emptyDp} alt="..." />
```

## Date Formatting

Use `moment` for relative timestamps:
```js
import moment from "moment";
moment(createdAt).fromNow() // "3 minutes ago"
```
